{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1092", "sample_idx": 41, "model_name": "meta/llama-4-maverick-17b-128e-instruct", "content": "My recent trip to Japan was a sensory overload in the best possible way. From the moment I stepped off the plane, I was struck by the unique blend of traditional and modern culture. The neon lights of Tokyo's city streets gave way to serene gardens and ancient temples, a juxtaposition that left me in awe.\n\nOne of the highlights of my trip was visiting the famous Tsukiji Fish Market in Tokyo. The sights and smells of the bustling market were overwhelming, but the highlight was definitely trying some of the freshest sushi I've ever had. I also had the opportunity to visit the Fushimi Inari shrine in Kyoto, famous for its thousands of vermilion torii gates that form a tunnel up the mountain. The hike was challenging, but the scenery was breathtaking.\n\nJapanese food was, of course, a major part of my trip. I sampled a variety of dishes, from ramen and udon noodles to tempura and yakitori. Each meal was a delicious and satisfying experience. The people I met along the way were also incredibly friendly and welcoming, making me feel at home despite the language barrier.\n\nOverall, my trip to Japan was an unforgettable experience that left me with a deep appreciation for the country's rich culture and history. I'm already planning my next trip back to this fascinating country.", "logprobs": [{"token": "My", "logprob": -0.46528711915016174}, {"token": " recent", "logprob": -0.00416210200637579}, {"token": " trip", "logprob": -7.152531907195225e-06}, {"token": " to", "logprob": 0.0}, {"token": " Japan", "logprob": -3.576278118089249e-07}, {"token": " was", "logprob": -6.556489552167477e-06}, {"token": " a", "logprob": -0.20399625599384308}, {"token": " sensory", "logprob": -1.5810136795043945}, {"token": " overload", "logprob": -0.035803280770778656}, {"token": " in", "logprob": -0.00021407696476671845}, {"token": " the", "logprob": -2.2649740